overview:
THE FORMAT, in full — one object with a "locales" array, one entry per language:

{
  "locales": [
    {
      "code": "fr",
      "displayName": "Français",
      "systemLanguage": "French",
      "strings": {
        "hud.greeting": "Bon retour, {0} !",
        "menu.quit": "Quitter",
        "menu.start": "Démarrer"
      }
    }
  ]
}

Four fields per language. `code` becomes the LocaleAsset's Id. `displayName` is what a language picker shows. `systemLanguage` is the NAME of a UnityEngine.SystemLanguage value — "French", "ChineseSimplified" — used to auto-pick this language on a matching device; leave it empty to opt out. `strings` is the key-to-text table.

usage.code:
// Read a bundle and turn it into the same table a CSV produces.
LocaleBundle bundle = LocalizationBundleJson.Parse(File.ReadAllText(path));
LocalizationTable table = LocalizationBundleJson.ToTable(bundle);

// Write one out, carrying the two things a table cannot hold.
LocaleBundle exported = LocalizationBundleJson.FromTable(table, displayNames, systemLanguages);
File.WriteAllText(path, LocalizationBundleJson.ToJson(exported));
